{% doc %}
  The low-level swatch renderer: one option value, one visual.

  ## Resolution order

  Seven sources, tried narrowest first. Each exists because the one after it is
  not good enough for someone, and the order matters more than the list:

  1. **Metaobject** — `option_value.swatch` pointing at a metaobject entry with
     its own colour, image and label. The richest source, and the one a merchant
     maintains once for a whole catalogue.
  2. **Shopify's native swatch** — a colour or image set on the option value in
     the admin. Per-product, survives a theme change, and is what Shopify itself
     uses in filters and search.
  3. **A variant metafield image** — the escape hatch for a pattern that is
     genuinely a photograph: marble, wood grain, printed fabric. A hex code for
     any of those is a lie.
  4. **The theme's swatch map** — `settings.swatch_config`. The practical option
     when option values are shared across a whole catalogue.
  5. **Gradients and dual tones**, from the same map. `Sunset=linear-gradient(...)`
     renders as written; `Navy/White=#292B6C/#ffffff` splits the circle. A
     two-colour product drawn as one colour is wrong in a way customers notice
     before they notice anything else.
  6. **CSS colour names** — `Dark red=darkred` works, because a merchant who
     writes a colour name means a colour.
  7. **The fallback** — the variant's own image, initials, or a text pill.

  ## Why the fallback is never nothing

  A value with no entry renders as a readable pill, never as an empty circle. An
  empty circle is indistinguishable from a white product, and a customer who
  cannot tell those apart clicks the wrong one.

  This snippet renders the *visual only* — `aria-hidden`, no name, no input.
  `swatch-input.liquid` wraps it in the accessible control. Keeping them apart is
  what lets the same visual appear in a filter checkbox, a card, and a radio
  group without three copies of the resolution logic.

  Parameters:
    value        (string, required)  The option value, e.g. "Mango"
    option_name  (string, optional)  The option's name, e.g. "Flavour"
    option_value (object, optional)  Shopify's option value drop, for native swatches
    variant      (variant, optional) Used by the variant-image fallback
    shape        (string, optional)  circle | round | portrait. Default from settings
    size         (string, optional)  small | medium | large. Default medium
    disabled     (boolean, optional) Draws the unavailable cross-out

  @example
    {% render 'swatch', value: value, option_name: option.name, option_value: value, size: 'small' %}
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign normalized = value | strip | downcase

  assign swatch_color = blank
  assign swatch_color_secondary = blank
  assign swatch_image = blank
  assign swatch_gradient = blank
  assign swatch_label = blank

  # ---- 1. Metaobject ------------------------------------------------------
  assign entry = option_value.swatch.metaobject
  if entry != blank
    if entry.color != blank
      assign swatch_color = entry.color
    endif
    if entry.image != blank
      assign swatch_image = entry.image | image_url: width: 120
    endif
    if entry.label != blank
      assign swatch_label = entry.label
    endif
  endif

  # ---- 2. Shopify's native swatch -----------------------------------------
  if swatch_color == blank and swatch_image == blank
    if option_value.swatch.color != blank
      assign swatch_color = option_value.swatch.color
    endif
    if option_value.swatch.image != blank
      assign swatch_image = option_value.swatch.image | image_url: width: 120
    endif
  endif

  # ---- 3. A variant metafield image ---------------------------------------
  if swatch_color == blank and swatch_image == blank
    assign meta_image = variant.metafields.custom.swatch_image
    if meta_image != blank
      assign swatch_image = meta_image | image_url: width: 120
    endif
  endif

  # ---- 4 to 6. The theme's swatch map -------------------------------------
  if swatch_color == blank and swatch_image == blank and settings.swatch_config != blank
    assign lines = settings.swatch_config | newline_to_br | split: '<br />'

    for line in lines
      assign raw = line | strip
      if raw == blank
        continue
      endif

      comment
        Split on the first '=' only, so a gradient containing '=' in a colour
        stop is not torn in half.
      endcomment
      assign pair = raw | split: '='
      if pair.size < 2
        continue
      endif

      assign entry_name = pair[0] | strip | downcase
      if entry_name != normalized
        continue
      endif

      assign entry_value = raw | remove_first: pair[0] | remove_first: '=' | strip

      if entry_value contains 'gradient('
        assign swatch_gradient = entry_value
      elsif entry_value contains '#' or entry_value contains 'rgb'
        assign tones = entry_value | split: '/'
        if tones.size > 1
          assign swatch_color = tones[0] | strip
          assign swatch_color_secondary = tones[1] | strip
        else
          assign swatch_color = entry_value
        endif
      elsif entry_value contains '.'
        comment
          Anything with a dot is a filename in Content > Files. `file_url`
          returns an empty string for a missing file, which the fallback catches.
        endcomment
        assign swatch_image = entry_value | file_url
      else
        comment
          A bare word is a CSS colour name. A merchant who writes "darkred"
          means a colour, and refusing it would send them to look up a hex code
          for no reason.
        endcomment
        assign swatch_color = entry_value
      endif

      break
    endfor
  endif

  # ---- 7. Fallback --------------------------------------------------------
  assign fallback = settings.swatch_fallback | default: 'variant-image'

  if swatch_color == blank and swatch_image == blank and swatch_gradient == blank
    if fallback == 'variant-image'
      if variant.image != blank
        assign swatch_image = variant.image | image_url: width: 120
      elsif variant.featured_media.preview_image != blank
        assign swatch_image = variant.featured_media.preview_image | image_url: width: 120
      endif
    endif
  endif

  assign has_visual = false
  if swatch_color != blank or swatch_image != blank or swatch_gradient != blank
    assign has_visual = true
  endif

  assign display_label = swatch_label | default: value
  assign initials = display_label | strip | truncate: 2, ''

  assign resolved_shape = shape | default: settings.swatch_shape | default: 'circle'
  assign resolved_size = size | default: 'medium'
-%}

<span
  class="swatch{% unless has_visual %} swatch--text{% endunless %}"
  data-shape="{{ resolved_shape }}"
  data-size="{{ resolved_size }}"
  {% if disabled %}data-disabled{% endif %}
  data-swatch-value="{{ value | escape }}"
  {% if option_name != blank %}data-swatch-option="{{ option_name | escape }}"{% endif %}
  style="
    {%- if swatch_color != blank %}--swatch-color: {{ swatch_color }};{% endif -%}
    {%- if swatch_color_secondary != blank %}--swatch-color-secondary: {{ swatch_color_secondary }};{% endif -%}
    {%- if swatch_gradient != blank %}--swatch-gradient: {{ swatch_gradient }};{% endif -%}
    {%- if swatch_image != blank %}--swatch-image: url('{{ swatch_image }}');{% endif -%}"
  aria-hidden="true"
>
  {%- unless has_visual -%}
    {%- if fallback == 'label' -%}
      {{ display_label }}
    {%- else -%}
      {{ initials }}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endunless -%}
</span>
